# Anomalous RDP Session Source

## Overview

Surfaces devices that initiate an RDP session for the first time within a rolling baseline period. The premise matches the WinRM version in [Anomalous WinRM Session Source](Anomalous_WinRM_Source_Device.md): look at where the session came from rather than where it landed, so that a compromised endpoint pivoting outward is visible even when the destination-side logon looks ordinary.

RDP is the harder of the two. Outbound 3389 from client endpoints is common in most environments, and a first-time occurrence frequently means somebody changed teams, picked up a new responsibility, or was handed access to a server they had not touched before. Expect to spend more time tuning this one, and expect the steady state to be a handful of rows per run rather than zero.

This is written as a hunting query, not a custom detection rule. See Why This Is a Hunt below.

